{"id": "1", "contents": "SAHIL SAINI  \nSenior Data Scientist · GenAI Specialist · ML Researcher  \nDelhi NCR | +91 -9318338806 | sahilsaini.9899@gmail.com | LinkedIn: www.linkedin.com/in/sahil -saini -3a420217a  \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY  \nData Scientist with 5 years of experience developing and optimizing production -grade GenAI and ML systems across maritime logistics \nand healthcare domains. Deep expertise in LLMs, RAG architectures, multi -agent systems, and classical ML with proven ability  to \ndesign novel solutions for complex data problems. Recognized nationally (AIR 5, Startup India) for technical innovation in AI /ML \nresearch and system design, delivering 95%+ model accuracy and measurable business impact through algorithmic excellence.  \nKEY ACHIEVEMENTS  \n• All-India Rank 5 , Startup India Grand Challenge RAG Hackathon (competing against 150+ startups)  \n• Recognized by Ministry of Ports, Shipping & Waterways  for SPARSH analytics platform; featured in ET Government as national digital \ntransformation case study  \n• Finalist , BhashaSetu Startup Challenge; empaneled with Ministry of Information & Broadcasting for multilingual AI translation (text, audio, \nvideo) across 10+ Indian languages  \n• 15+ Impact & Innovation Awards  at Carelon Global Solutions —recognized for technical expertise, algorithmic innovation, and model \nperformance ($400K+ savings)  \n• Invented \"Intelligent Chunking\"  preprocessing pipeline using semantic segmentation and context -aware splitting, saving $15/claim across \n15K+ annual claims ($225K+ cumulative impact)  \nCORE TECHNICAL COMPETENCIES  \nGenAI & LLMs:  GPT -4, GPT -4o-mini, RAG · Prompt Engineering · Multi -Agent Systems · Vector Databases (FAISS, Chroma, Pinecone)  · Embeddings  \nML/DL:  PyTorch · TensorFlow · Scikit -learn · Hugging Face Transformers · Feature Engineering · Hyperparameter Optimization  \nData Science:  Statistical Analysis · Hypothesis Testing · A/B Testing · Time Series Analysis · Optimization Algorithms · Experimental Desig n \nTools & Platforms:  Python · SQL · PostgreSQL · MongoDB · Azure · MLflow · FastAPI · Streamlit · Dash  \nMathematics:  Linear Algebra · Probability Theory · Statistical Inference · Optimization · Mathematical Modeling  \nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE  \nSenior Data Scientist  \nAI Transmute Pvt. Ltd., Noida (NCR)  \nDec 2024 – Present  \nSAMVAAD AI – Conversational Analytics for Tabular Data  \n• Architected metadata -driven multi -agent LLM system with specialized agents (Query Parser → Decomposer → Code Generator → Ambiguity \nResolver) enabling natural language queries on 50GB+ datasets with 95%+ accuracy  \n• Designed novel hallucination elimination approach using Pandas execution grounding and validation layers; achieved 3 -4 sec query latency \nprocessing 200+ daily queries  \n• Developed prompt engineering framework with chain -of-thought reasoning for complex multi -table SQL generation, handling joins, \naggregations, and nested queries  \n• Implemented context window optimization techniques to handle large -context limits while preserving semantic accuracy across multi -table \nqueries  \n• Reduced data analysis time by 80% (from 30 -min manual SQL → 3 -sec NL queries), achieving 95%+ user satisfaction on complex analytical \nqueries  \nTAPAS – Tug & Pilot Allocation System  \n• Designed multi -objective optimization engine integrating vessel schedules, weather constraints, resource availability, and crew fatigue \nregulations using mixed -integer programming  \n• Developed mathematical models translating domain constraints (tide windows, draft restrictions, crew regulations) into optimi zation \nobjectives with 20+ variables  \n• Built constraint satisfaction algorithms balancing competing objectives: minimizing vessel wait time vs. crew utilization vs.  operational costs  \n• Achieved 15% reduction in vessel turnaround time and 20% improvement in resource utilization through algorithmic optimization  \nSPARSH – Smart Port Analytics & Reporting Hub  • Conducted exploratory data analysis across 50+ disparate data streams (vessel movements, cargo handling, weather, equipment t elemetry) \nto identify correlation patterns and operational bottlenecks  \n• Architected 3 -tier analytics system: Executive dashboards → Root cause analysis (drill -down across interconnected metrics) → Predictive ML \nmodels for bottleneck forecasting  \n• Developed GenAI narrative generation engine using GPT -4 to auto -generate natural language summaries explaining metric deviations, \nanomalies, and operational trends  \n• Built time series forecasting models (ARIMA, Prophet) predicting port congestion and equipment failures with 85%+ accuracy  \n• Designed anomaly detection algorithms identifying operational inefficiencies, reducing incident response time by 40%  \nData Scientist → Senior Data Scientist  \nCarelon Global Solutions (Elevance Health), Gurgaon  \nJul 2021 – Dec 2024  \nICA Engine – Intelligent Claims Assistant  \n• Architected GenAI system using GPT -4 with custom RAG pipeline for healthcare claims validation, processing 2,500+ annual claims with 98% \naccuracy  \n• Designed modular prompt engineering framework with 15+ specialized templates for different claim types (inpatient, outpatient , emergency, \npharmacy)  \n• Built MongoDB -based prompt versioning system enabling A/B testing and experiment tracking; improved prompt performance by 23% through \niterative optimization  \n• Developed intelligent document parsing algorithms combining OCR output with semantic understanding to extract structured data  from \nunstructured medical records  \n• Reduced claims validation time by 92% (from 1 -3 hours → 5 -10 minutes) through algorithmic automation, delivering $400K+ annual savings  \nVALID – DRG Verification Pipeline  \n• Implemented 4 -stage ML pipeline: OCR preprocessing → document understanding → prompt engineering → evidence extraction with \ncoordinate -based highlighting  \n• Developed \"Intelligent Chunking\" algorithm using semantic segmentation, sentence boundary detection, and context -aware splitting for \noptimal LLM processing  \n• Achieved 93% extraction accuracy on complex medical documents through custom prompt templates and few -shot learning strategies  \n• Built coordinate -based evidence highlighting system using computer vision techniques, reducing auditor review time by 40%  \n• Designed quality metrics and evaluation framework measuring extraction accuracy, hallucination rates, and clinical validity  \nResponsible AI & Model Monitoring Research  \n• Researched and formalized statistical drift detection methodologies (Kolmogorov -Smirnov, Population Stability Index) for healthcare ML \nmodels  \n• Developed fairness testing framework using Chi -square tests and demographic parity metrics to detect bias in model predictions across \npatient subgroups  \n• Designed algorithmic monitoring library implementing data drift, concept drift, and performance degradation detection across 40+ production \nmodels  \n• Reduced model degradation detection time from weeks to hours through automated statistical testing and alerting algorithms  \nEDUCATION  \nMaster of Statistics (M.S.)  \nIndian Institute of Technology (IIT) Kanpur | 2019 – 2021 | CGPA: 7.2/10  \nB.Sc. Statistics (Hons.)  \nUniversity of Delhi | 2016 – 2019 | CGPA: 7.8/10  Sahil_Resume_tech.pdf"}
